# Zarr to Nx

Convert a whole array, a stored chunk, or a rectangular region into an `Nx.Tensor`.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:ex_zarr, "~> 1.3"},
  # {:ex_zarr, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "../../..")},
  {:nx, "~> 0.7"}
])
```

## Setup

```elixir
alias ExZarr.Array

{:ok, array} =
  Array.create(shape: {6, 4}, chunks: {4, 2}, dtype: :float32, storage: :memory)

binary = for i <- 0..23, into: <<>>, do: <<i * 1.0::float-little-32>>
:ok = Array.set_slice(array, binary, start: {0, 0}, stop: {6, 4})

{:ok, nx_type} = ExZarr.Nx.zarr_to_nx_type(array.metadata.dtype)
nx_type
```

## Whole array

```elixir
{:ok, tensor} = ExZarr.Nx.to_tensor(array, names: [:rows, :cols])
{Nx.shape(tensor), Nx.type(tensor), Nx.names(tensor)}
```

## Round trip

```elixir
{:ok, stored} =
  ExZarr.Nx.from_tensor(Nx.iota({8}, type: {:s, 32}),
    storage: :memory,
    chunks: {3}
  )

{:ok, back} = ExZarr.Nx.to_tensor(stored)
Nx.to_flat_list(back)
```

## Dtypes that Zarr does not store

`{:bf, 16}`, `{:f, 16}`, and complex types return `{:error, message}` from `nx_to_zarr_type/1`. Store float32 and cast in memory when you need those types.
